    "## Assignment Questions & Solutions\n",
    "\n",
    "### Question 1: One-Tailed Hypothesis Test (Is Strategy B Better?)\n",
    "\n",
    "The marketing director at GlobalGadgets is optimistic and believes that Strategy B has increased customer spending compared to Strategy A. They want to test this claim.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Problem Statement:** Test if the average daily spending under Strategy B ($\mu_B$) is significantly greater than the average daily spending under Strategy A ($\mu_A$). Use a significance level ($\alpha$) of 0.05.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Hypotheses:**\n",
    "* **Null Hypothesis ($H_0$):** $\\mu_B \\leq \\mu_A$ (Strategy B spending is less than or equal to Strategy A spending)\n",
    "* **Alternative Hypothesis ($H_1$):** $\\mu_B > \\mu_A$ (Strategy B spending is greater than Strategy A spending)\n",
    "\n",
    "This is a **right-tailed test**.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Excel Steps:**\n",
    "1. Go to the **Data** tab and click **Data Analysis**.\n",
    "2. Select **t-Test: Two-Sample Assuming Unequal Variances** and click **OK**.\n",
    "3. For **Variable 1 Range**, select Strategy A data (A1:A31).\n",
    "4. For **Variable 2 Range**, select Strategy B data (B1:B31).\n",
    "5. Set **Hypothesized Mean Difference** to 0, check **Labels**, and set **Alpha** to 0.05.\n",
    "6. Click **OK**.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Expected Excel Output & Interpretation:**\n",
    "* **t Stat:** -3.21\n",
    "* **P(T<=t) one-tail:** 0.0010\n",
    "* **t Critical one-tail:** 1.672\n",
    "\n",
    "**Decision Rule:** If $P(T \\leq t)$ one-tail $< \\alpha$, reject $H_0$.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Conclusion:** In this example, the p-value 0.0010 is much smaller than $\\alpha = 0.05$. Therefore, we **reject the null hypothesis**. There is sufficient evidence to conclude that Strategy B spending is significantly greater than Strategy A.\n",
    "\n",
    "---"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Question 2: Two-Tailed Hypothesis Test (Is There Any Difference?)\n",
    "\n",
    "The finance department wants to know if there is simply any significant difference without assuming one is better.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Problem Statement:** Test if there is a significant difference between Strategy A ($\mu_A$) and Strategy B ($\mu_B$). Use a significance level ($\alpha$) of 0.01.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Hypotheses:**\n",
    "* **Null Hypothesis ($H_0$):** $\\mu_A = \\mu_B$\n",
    "* **Alternative Hypothesis ($H_1$):** $\\mu_A \\neq \\mu_B$\n",
    "\n",
    "This is a **two-tailed test**.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Expected Excel Output:**\n",
    "\n",
    "| t-Test: Two-Sample Assuming Unequal Variances | Strategy A | Strategy B |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| Mean | 49.62 | 55.45 |\n",
    "| Variance | 57.08 | 69.87 |\n",
    "| Observations | 30 | 30 |\n",
    "| Hypothesized Mean Difference | 0 | |\n",
    "| df | 57 | |\n",
    "| **t Stat** | **-3.21** | |\n",
    "| P(T<=t) one-tail | 0.0010 | |\n",
    "| t Critical one-tail | 2.396 | |\n",
    "| **P(T<=t) two-tail** | **0.0020** | |\n",
    "| **t Critical two-tail** | **2.664** | |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Decision Rule:** If $P(T \\leq t)$ two-tail $< \\alpha$, reject $H_0$.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Conclusion:** The p-value 0.0020 is smaller than $\\alpha = 0.01$. We **reject the null hypothesis**. There is a significant difference in spending between Strategy A and Strategy B.\n",
    "\n",
    "---"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Question 3: Significance Level and Practical Implications\n",
    "\n",
    "**Problem Statement:**\n",
    "1. Re-evaluate Question 1 if $\\alpha = 0.001$.\n",
    "2. Calculate the absolute difference in means and discuss practical significance.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Re-evaluating with $\\alpha = 0.001$:**\n",
    "The p-value is 0.0010. Comparison: $0.0010 < 0.001$? **No.** We would **fail to reject** the null hypothesis at this stricter level.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Absolute Difference:**\n",
    "$|\\bar{x}_B - \\bar{x}_A| = |55.45 - 49.62| = 5.83$ USD.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Discussion on Practical Significance:**\n",
    "A difference of $5.83 USD per customer is statistically significant, but practical significance depends on:\n",
    "* **Scale:** With millions of customers, this is a massive revenue boost.\n",
    "* **Costs:** If Strategy B is expensive to run, the $5.83 increase might not cover costs.\n",
    "* **Other factors:** Retention and brand perception also matter.\n",
    "\n",
    "Conclusion: Practical significance requires further business analysis beyond the t-test."
   ]
  }
